{"version":1,"slug":"neural-networks","topic":"How does a neural network learn?","level":"intermediate","title":"How Neural Networks Learn","summary":"You will understand how a neural network makes a prediction, measures its error, and adjusts its weights to improve.","scopeNote":null,"scenes":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","title":"How does a neural network learn?","segments":[{"id":"intro-0","narration":"How does a neural network learn? Let's find out, one step at a time.","sig":"o_z-wSNOCLqlVEbjVCTs18PJNupa4CyK","actions":[]},{"id":"intro-1","narration":"How can a computer learn to recognize a handwritten number without anyone ever writing a single rule for it?","sig":"9pwKfL_bDh1FzzdjaMt_IBy-8rSU4d0N","actions":[{"id":"hero","kind":"icon","cue":"How can a","text":"Neural Network","items":null,"icon":"network","at":{"col":0,"row":1,"w":4,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"intro-2","narration":"Here's our plan. First, Guesses and Mistakes. Then, The Learning Loop. And finally, A Worked Example.","sig":"vbkzIkv0_BVufnqW3K_jDmPaYf_EvS7Y","actions":[{"id":"agenda","kind":"timeline","cue":"Here's our plan","text":null,"items":["1: Guesses and Mistakes","2: The Learning Loop","3: A Worked Example"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":5,"row":1,"w":7,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c1","kind":"chapter","title":"Guesses and Mistakes","segments":[{"id":"c1-0","narration":"Imagine a neural network trying to tell cats from dogs. At first, it has no idea, so it just makes a random guess.","sig":"hWPPjxyTmkHNCb_dqHJVYeDc2yr0QP8i","actions":[{"id":"net","kind":"box","cue":"neural network","text":"Neural Network","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":1,"row":1,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"guess","kind":"box","cue":"random guess","text":"Random Guess: Dog","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":5,"row":1,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"a1","kind":"arrow","cue":"random guess","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"net","to":"guess","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-1","narration":"Next, it compares that guess to the true label, which is cat. The difference between the two is the error, which we call the loss.","sig":"r0492k-E2wYF3EXS76tmcomU0PS-_jJn","actions":[{"id":"truth","kind":"box","cue":"true label","text":"True Label: Cat","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":5,"row":4,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"loss","kind":"circle","cue":"call the loss","text":"Error (Loss)","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":9,"row":2,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"red","expr":null},{"id":"a2","kind":"arrow","cue":"call the loss","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"guess","to":"loss","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null},{"id":"a3","kind":"arrow","cue":"call the loss","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"truth","to":"loss","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-2","narration":"Many people think the network simply memorizes the right answers. In reality, it uses that loss to adjust its internal weights, so its next guess is closer.","sig":"pHk5XdCZmXgMly-F0mpORttm94FxTdpC","actions":[{"id":"wrong","kind":"note","cue":"memorizes the right","text":"Memorizes answers","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":1,"row":4,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"red","expr":null},{"id":"x1","kind":"cross_out","cue":"memorizes the right","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"wrong","color":"red","expr":null},{"id":"right","kind":"note","cue":"adjust its internal","text":"Adjusts weights","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":9,"row":4,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"c1","kind":"check","cue":"adjust its internal","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"right","color":"green","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c2","kind":"chapter","title":"The Learning Loop","segments":[{"id":"c2-0","narration":"Once the network measures its error, it needs to use that mistake to improve. It does this through a continuous learning loop: first it makes a guess, then it measures the loss.","sig":"dmxkrycL-sD7_74jV5zk2lxk0cR7Nbo4","actions":[{"id":"loop","kind":"cycle","cue":"continuous learning loop","text":null,"items":["Guess","Measure Loss","Nudge Weights","Repeat"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":0,"w":6,"h":5},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":null,"expr":null},{"id":"p1","kind":"pulse","cue":"measures the loss","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"loop[1]","color":"red","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-1","narration":"Next, backpropagation traces the error backward through the network to see which weights caused it. Then gradient descent nudges those weights in the direction that reduces the error.","sig":"Lq0cs35Y62ZNp4dTylB7jVTR7DvrqxFp","actions":[{"id":"t1","kind":"trace","cue":"traces the error","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"loop","color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"h1","kind":"highlight","cue":"nudges those weights","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"loop[2]","color":"orange","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-2","narration":"As the network repeats this cycle thousands of times, the overall loss drops steadily, just like a ball rolling downhill.","sig":"L7f3FNbKugQoH7PKV-IboRUJufYxbpTy","actions":[{"id":"loss_plot","kind":"plot","cue":"overall loss drops","text":"Loss over time","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":6,"row":1,"w":6,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":"2^(-x); 0..5"},{"id":"c1","kind":"callout","cue":"rolling downhill","text":"Gradient descent","items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"loss_plot","color":"green","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c3","kind":"chapter","title":"A Worked Example","segments":[{"id":"c3-0","narration":"Let us see that learning loop in action with one simple neuron. Suppose it takes four hours studied and multiplies by a starting weight of ten.","sig":"x-5MxI9omQm43f6y_MAjW8RMW3eD1BiQ","actions":[{"id":"neuron","kind":"sketch","cue":"one simple neuron","text":"Weight = 10","items":["circle 50 50 32","text 50 45 × 10","text 50 65 Neuron"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":0,"w":3,"h":3},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"ink","expr":null},{"id":"hours","kind":"box","cue":"four hours studied","text":"Hours studied: 4","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":1,"w":3,"h":1},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"a1","kind":"arrow","cue":"multiplies by a starting","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"hours","to":"neuron","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-1","narration":"It guesses a score of forty percent, but the actual score is eighty percent.","sig":"MvUi-fCdPnssossIzLcdmzMP0d7tLlQk","actions":[{"id":"pred","kind":"box","cue":"forty percent","text":"Guess: 40%","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":8,"row":1,"w":3,"h":1},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"a2","kind":"arrow","cue":"forty percent","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"neuron","to":"pred","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null},{"id":"actual","kind":"box","cue":"eighty percent","text":"Actual: 80%","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":8,"row":3,"w":3,"h":1},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-2","narration":"The error is forty points too low, so gradient descent nudges the weight upward.","sig":"pGi8souvvABsHnD7r8qP3ez3iw1BVS-U","actions":[{"id":"err","kind":"note","cue":"forty points too low","text":"Error: 40 too low","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":4,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"red","expr":null},{"id":"a3","kind":"arrow","cue":"forty points too low","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"pred","to":"err","target":null,"color":"red","expr":null},{"id":"a4","kind":"arrow","cue":"nudges the weight upward","text":"Nudge up","items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"err","to":"neuron","target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"t1","kind":"trace","cue":"nudges the weight upward","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"a4","color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-3","narration":"With a new weight of fifteen, the next guess will be much closer to the truth.","sig":"O_L1t58bEh3Z47WMqiWOaAaLOFCsb6pB","actions":[{"id":"new_w","kind":"callout","cue":"new weight of fifteen","text":"New weight: 15","items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"neuron","color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"p1","kind":"pulse","cue":"new weight of fifteen","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"neuron","color":"green","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"recap","kind":"recap","title":"Recap","segments":[{"id":"recap-0","narration":"So, a neural network learns by guessing, measuring its loss, and nudging its weights with gradient descent. Over thousands of rounds, its guesses get sharper. What part would you like to explore next?","sig":"dtUhuRYoQNxpkcMxsCd2y0wwyz4vgkj-","actions":[{"id":"takeaways","kind":"list","cue":"guessing, measuring its loss","text":null,"items":["Guesses and measures loss","Backpropagation traces the error","Gradient descent nudges weights"],"icon":"circle-check","at":{"col":1,"row":1,"w":6,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"brain_icon","kind":"icon","cue":"guesses get sharper","text":"Sharper guesses","items":null,"icon":"brain","at":{"col":8,"row":2,"w":3,"h":3},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]}]}],"quiz":[{"question":"What does a neural network actually adjust when it learns from a mistake?","options":["Its internal weights","The training labels","Its memorized answers","The input data"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Instead of memorizing answers, the network uses the loss to adjust its internal weights so future guesses are closer.","chapter":1},{"question":"What is the role of backpropagation in the learning loop?","options":["It makes the first guess","It traces error to weights","It deletes wrong guesses","It stores the final score"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Backpropagation traces the error backward through the network to identify which weights caused it.","chapter":2},{"question":"In our example, the neuron guessed forty percent instead of eighty percent. How did it improve?","options":["It lowered the weight","It changed the hours studied","It nudged the weight upward","It ignored the error"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Because the guess was too low, gradient descent nudged the weight upward from ten to fifteen.","chapter":3}],"suggestions":["How deep neural networks work","What is overfitting in machine learning?","How do activation functions work?"],"models":{"lesson":"google/gemini-4-hydrogen","voice":"google/gemini-3.8-flash-tts"},"createdAt":"2026-11-17T17:40:22.792Z","audioBase":"/samples/neural-networks"}